          "maxclass": "comment",
          "numinlets": 1,
          "numoutlets": 0,
          "patching_rect": [
            25.0,
            58.0,
            1110.0,
            60.0
          ],
          "text": "Use this as a model library for a separate timed score. Open a category, unlock, select a complete p Cue_\u2026 object, copy, and paste it into your score. Its inlet accepts score data; its internal forward sends to the v15 engine."
        }
      },
      {
        "box": {
          "id": "syntax",
          "maxclass": "comment",
          "numinlets": 1,
          "numoutlets": 0,
          "patching_rect": [
            25.0,
            125.0,
            1110.0,
            45.0
          ],
          "text": "Continuous: value ramp_ms \u2022 Integer/menu: value \u2022 Action: bang \u2022 Partial: index value ramp_ms \u2022 Family: root 0/1. Use stop to cancel a copied cue\u2019s ramp. Bare continuous values use 20 ms."
        }
      },
      {
        "box": {
          "id": "timing",
          "maxclass": "comment",
          "numinlets": 1,
          "numoutlets": 0,
          "patching_rect": [
            25.0,
            175.0,
            1110.0,
            45.0
          ],
          "text": "Schedule cue inputs with delay, pipe, metro/counter, or your preferred score system. Keep one active writer per variable. The destination names are shared across open v15 engine instances."
        }
      },
